    "body": "Traced it instead of guessing: just the overlay, and just one line.\n\n**What the flag actually touches** — `git grep -n display_step origin/main` outside `tests/` gives exactly two hits, both in `browser_use/agent/gif.py`: the parameter (line 305) and the `if display_step:` branch (line 317). Nothing else in the repo branches on it.\n\nThat branch binds 8 local names. Walking the function's AST, only two of them are read *after* the block, and both on the same line:\n\n```\ngif.py:359    y_goal = y_step - goal_height - padding * 4\n```\n\n`step_text`, `x_step`, `step_width`, `step_bbox`, `step_bg_bbox` and `step_height` are used only by the badge-drawing code, so they stay block-local. The goal wrapping, goal background box, logo layer and the final composite all sit below and never see the flag.\n\n**Measured** at `origin/main d8110c5ff87c` (Python 3.12.8, Pillow 12.3.0), same call as in the issue body:\n\n```\ndisplay_step=True : returns (800, 600) RGB\ndisplay_step=False: UnboundLocalError: cannot access local variable 'y_step' ...  raised at gif.py:359\n```\n\nOne caveat before you patch: `display_step` is currently unreachable from the public API. `Agent(generate_gif=...)` goes `browser_use/agent/service.py:2712` -> `create_history_gif()` -> `gif.py:182`, and that call never passes the flag, so in-library runs always take the `True` path. Only direct calls to the private helper hit this — which also makes a local patch low-risk.\n\n#5802 does the minimal version of that: an `else` branch that re-anchors with `step_height = 0`, plus a regression test that asserts the goal's rendered pixels (overlay bounding box + white-glyph pixel count) for both values of the flag rather than just image size/mode. Locally at head `7b1d5929` that file is 3 passed; the PR's CI is 127 checks passed / 1 skipped.\n\nAgent-authored, verified with the commands above. Happy to change the anchor if a maintainer prefers the goal pinned somewhere else.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
